---
type: crash-investigation
title: Codex app-server TUI startup crash
description: Verified Bob and Walkie crash caused by a persisted compaction callback using an unsupported remote launch identity.
timestamp: 2026-10-20
tags: [codex, app-server, tui, restart, crash]
---

# Observed

Bob's aap-bob-next logs for installed version
0.2.51-nightly.20261020-165616.9ac82f0 repeatedly recorded
`codex_remote_launch_failed error=KeyError: 'codex-remote'` at 2026-10-21
03:32:14, 03:38:04 and earlier retries. The plain Codex TUI did not show this
failure. The local `G:/ciel-Walkie` workspace also had a durable automatic
`channel-compact-request.json` while its router log recorded context-recovery
and deferred compaction activity.

The pure reproduction was run without a Codex process, network, or terminal:
`RemoteMemorySynchronizer.project_current_pointer("codex-remote")` reached
`remote_memory.py:619` and raised `KeyError` because `RUNTIME_FILES` has
`codex-app-server` but not `codex-remote`.

# Trace

`_run_tui` enters the terminal polling loop. A pending session command calls
`ciel_runtime.py:_inject_pending_compact_request`, which refreshed remote
instructions using `last_launch_runtime()`. Launch-state normalization returns
`codex-remote` for `codex-remote-router`. Remote memory then indexed
`RUNTIME_FILES["codex-remote"]`; the broad remote launch exception boundary
reported this as `codex_remote_launch_failed` and returned exit code 1. A durable
request caused the same failure on each subsequent restart.

The CLI dispatch map was not the failing boundary. The error occurred after the
remote TUI had already entered its terminal loop.

# Change

Added `instruction_runtime()` to map persisted `codex-remote` and
`codex-desktop` identities to the existing `codex-app-server` instruction
runtime before pre-compaction synchronization. Unsupported direct pointer
projection now raises the typed `ValueError` instead of leaking `KeyError`; the
existing synchronization wrappers log it and continue. Added regression tests
for alias normalization, the original compact callback, RPC ownership of the
remote TUI compact action, and the typed unsupported-runtime boundary.

# Verification

Focused isolated evidence:
- `evidence/before.txt`: expected failing regressions (4 errors), including the
  original KeyError and missing helper.
- `evidence/after.txt`: 259 tests passed, 80 skipped.
- `evidence/adjacent.txt`: 115 tests passed.
- `evidence/final.txt`: 260 tests passed, 80 skipped.
- Python compileall passed for the changed production and test files.
- Architecture budget returned no violations.
- Pure alias reproduction returned `codex-remote -> codex-app-server` and the
  direct unsupported boundary returned `ValueError`.
- Native acceptance `run-codex-remote-startup-crash-fix-142024` passed: the app-server
  TUI restarted, Leave paused was dismissed, paused goal identity/objective/status/
  updatedAt stayed unchanged, post-restart notification reached the fixture, the old
  native process ended, and app-server listener release was observed.

# Scope

No Bob or Walkie process was restarted or modified. The fix is local source
work only until review, commit, and release verification are explicitly carried
out.
